    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0086" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg36"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/274</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-20T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                                1918, 8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2089. Your 2369, February 14, 2 [12] p.m., and referring Department’s
                        2065.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d54-f1"/> We desire progress with Bolshevik
                    authorities to be gradual. I do not believe that joint protests are wise and am
                    glad to learn your judgment has prompted you to refrain from further action this
                    character without express authority.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
